{"chunk_id": "9caa2a655f61", "text": "As Rama and Lakshmana travel with the sage Vishwamitra, they reach the beautiful city of Vishala. At Rama\u2019s request, Vishwamitra recounts a cosmic legend he once heard from Indra: the churning of the Ocean of Milk. Devas and asuras, seeking immortality, use Mount Mandara as a churning rod and the serpent Vasuki as a rope. The process releases a catastrophic poison that threatens the universe until Shiva compassionately drinks it. Vishnu then supports the sinking mountain in the form of a tortoise. From the ocean emerge wonders\u2014Dhanvantari, countless apsaras, Varuni, the celestial horse Uchchaishravas, the Kaustubha jewel, and finally the nectar of immortality\u2014triggering a fierce battle in which Vishnu, as the enchantress Mohini, secures victory for the gods.\nVishwamitra narrates the churning of the ocean, Shiva drinking poison, Vishnu supporting Mandara as Kurma, and the devas\u2019 eventual victory for the nectar.\nThemes: churning of the ocean, divine cooperation and conflict, Shiva drinking poison, Vishnu avatars, quest for immortality", "vector": [0.014068991877138615, -0.022894209250807762, -0.004743723664432764, 0.003841605270281434, -0.02127242460846901, 0.018204545602202415, -0.031111257150769234, -0.006000607740134001, -0.018528902903199196, -0.03451700881123543, 0.015852956101298332, 0.02261039800941944, 0.012528295628726482, -0.004774131812155247, -0.007385883014649153, 0.008223805576562881, 0.039977021515369415, -0.011589011177420616, 0.02277257665991783, -0.009865864180028439, -0.013339187949895859, -0.003679426619783044, 0.020123658701777458, 0.0003720815875567496, -0.015298846177756786, 0.008575192652642727, 0.019853360950946808, -0.02755684405565262, -0.004294353537261486, -0.010048314929008484, 0.009629352949559689, 0.01571780815720558, 0.008987396024167538, 0.0024056490510702133, -0.010832177475094795, 0.002753657288849354, 0.008595464751124382, -0.01387978345155716, -0.001436800928786397, -0.00